#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:855
msgid ""
"The table shows all the parameters that need to be provided to the ``model`` "
"(in this case DFN). For example, we see that we need to define (amongst "
"others) the ``Negative electrode thickness [m]``, which is defined to be a "
"``Parameter``. This means it can only have a constant value. In contrast, "
"other parameters are defined to be a ``FunctionParameter``, which means that "
"they can depend on model variables. For example, the ``Current function "
"[A]`` is a ``FunctionParameter`` that can depend on ``Time [s]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:858
msgid ""
"Note that a ``FunctionParameter`` can always be defined to be a constant (i."
"e. like if it was a ``Parameter``), but a ``Parameter`` cannot be defined to "
"be a function. This is because these dependencies are hardcoded in the model "
"definitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:870
msgid "Constant parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:872
msgid ""
"Let's start with a simple example: change the ``Current function [A]`` to be "
"10 A. To do this, we can simply update the value in the dictionary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:-1
msgid "[8]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:-1
msgid "parameter_values[\"Current function [A]\"] = 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:893
msgid ""
"Note that, as we mentioned above, even though ``Current function [A]`` could "
"depend on time, we can always define it to be a function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:895
msgid "Now we just need to run the simulation with the new parameter values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:-1
msgid "[9]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-4-setting-parameter-values.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"sim = pybamm.Simulation(model, parameter_values=parameter_values)\n"
"sim.solve([0, 3600])\n"
"sim.plot()"
msgstr ""

